    "claim_id": "c8",
    "verdict": "SUPPORTED",
    "reasoning": "Passage [6] states warnings begin when oldest XIDs reach 'forty million transactions from the wraparound point'. Passage [7] states the system refuses new XIDs when there are 'fewer than three million transactions left until wraparound'. The difference between 40 million and 3 million is 37 million transactions.",
